# DTF tier manifest: repo-read-hiding
#   (artifact-keeper#4418, #4473, #4498; all in 1.11.0, RED on 1.10.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. The read gates live in REST handlers ahead
# of storage; the oracle is pure HTTP plus direct DB reads for setup checks.
#
# THE BUGS
#   #4418  GET /api/v1/promotion/repositories/{key}/promotion-history needed
#          only a signed-in caller, so any user read the promotion history of
#          a private repository. Fixed: the existence-hiding read gate (404 as
#          for a missing repository), and the key of a counterpart repository
#          the caller cannot read is returned as "".
#   #4473  GET .../{key}/release-target needed only a signed-in caller: any
#          user read a private staging repository's link, and the 400 "only
#          available for staging repositories" told it the repository's type.
#          Fixed: the same gate, before the type check; a linked release
#          repository the caller cannot read is reported linked:true with key
#          and id null.
#   #4498  An unreadable repository answered `Repository '<key>' not found`
#          and a missing one `Repository not found`: same status, different
#          body, an existence oracle. Fixed: both return
#          {"code":"NOT_FOUND","message":"Repository not found"}.
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (FIX)     signed-in non-reader AND anonymous: GET /repositories/{private}
#             and its /artifacts and /storage are byte-identical to the same
#             path on a missing key and equal the shipped body; non-reader
#             promotion-history and release-target on a private staging repo
#             are 404 with the missing-repository body; release-target on a
#             private NON-staging repo is that 404, not the 400; the public
#             staging repo's history blanks its private counterpart's key and
#             its release-target hides the private link's key and id.
#   (CONTROL) on both images: missing key 404; reader and admin read the
#             repository, its history (with the counterpart key) and its link;
#             admin still gets the 400 on a non-staging repo; the listing
#             omits private repositories.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~40 back-to-back calls from three principals.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
